  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Amzad Naushad Sayyad vs The State Of Maharashtra on 17 November, 2025 2025:Bhc-Aug:31564 40 Aba No. 1734 Of 2 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1734 Of 2025 Amzad Naushad Sayyad Versus The State Of Maharashtra ... Mr. Arvind Ramnath Kawade, Advocate for Applicant Mr. P. D. Patil, App for Respondent - State ...",
    "facts": "Looking to the allegations that the applicant was found in possession of contraband pan masala and scented tobacco, which stand prohibited under the notification issued by the Commissioner of Food Safety under Section 30 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, and in view of the invocation of Section 328 of the IPC, it is noted that the contraband Gutkha and pan masala have already been seized by the Investigating Officer. The applicant has no criminal antecedents. Nothing further remains to be recovered from him, and he has expressed willingness to co-operate with the investigation and has also undertaken not to indulge in similar offences in future.",
